          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            %em super-scheme
            is the generalization of that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            is a space locally modeled on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            (i.e. an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+algebra"} supercommutative algebra
            (i.e. on affine superschemes, def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AffineSuperSchemes"}
            below).
          %h3#affine_superschemes Affine superschemes
          %p
            The following is a detailed and conceptual introduction of the concept of affine super-schemes. This is taken from
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+superalgebra"} geometry of physics – superalgebra
          %p
            The key idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
            is that it is nothing but plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            but “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"}> internalized
            ” not in ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
            and ef.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
            below.
          %p
            The key idea then of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            is to define super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            to be spaces whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            or a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %em characterized dually
            via their algebras of functions, and hence it makes sense to generalize the latter.
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
            statement is the following:
          #EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoRAlgebras.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras"}> embedding of smooth manifolds into formal duals of R-algebras
                )
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi SmoothMfd
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(-) \;\colon\; SmoothMfd \longrightarrow Alg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+countable+topological+space"} second countable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of) its
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %p
              In other words, for two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              and the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ←
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)\leftarrow C^\infty(Y)
          %p
            A
            %strong proof
            is for instance in (
            %a{:href => "embedding+of+smooth+manifolds+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras#KolarSlovakMichor93"}> Kolar-Slovak-Michor 93, lemma 35.8, corollaries 35.9, 35.10
            ).
          %p
            This says that we may
            %em identify
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            as the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"}> formal duals
            ” of certain
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} associative algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            to a generalized kind of manifold, defined thereby. Given any associative algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A)
            which is such that it has
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            as its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
            between certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
            is profound. In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            it has always been used implicitly, in fact it was so ingrained into theoretical physics that it took much effort to abstract away from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+system"} coordinate functions
            to discover global
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+geometry"} Riemannian geometry
            in the guise of“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"}> general relativity
            ”. As mathematics, an early prominent duality theorem is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            (between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
            are nothing but the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+algebras"} non-commutative algebras
            here yields
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+geometry"} non-commutative geometry
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} Isbell duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copresheaves"} copresheaves
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            we are concerned with spaces that are formally dual to associative algebras which are “very mildly” non-commutative, namely
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
            when viewed internal to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
            below). The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
            spaces are, depending on some technical details,
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+schemes"} super schemes
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            literature, such spaces are usually just called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspaces"} superspaces
          %p We now make this precise.
          #MonoidsInMonoidalCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              (def
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+category"} monoid internal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \;\colon\; 1 \longrightarrow A
                  (called the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
              %li
                %p
                  a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \;\colon\; A \otimes A \longrightarrow A
                  (called the
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %em product
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"}> associativity
                  ) the following
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %munderover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mo ≃
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi a
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi A
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi A
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi μ
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi μ
                                      %mo ⊗
                                      %mi A
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi μ
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi μ
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        (A\otimes A) \otimes A
                        \&amp;\underoverset{\simeq}{a_{A,A,A}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes (A \otimes A)
                        \&amp;\overset{A \otimes \mu}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes A
                        \\\
                        {}^{\mathllap{\mu \otimes A}}\downarrow
                        \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                        \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mu}}
                        \\\
                        A \otimes A
                        \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                        \&amp;\overset{\mu}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A
                        }
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associator"} associator
                  isomorphism of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li#UnitalityMonoid
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"}> unitality
                  ) the following
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi e
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi id
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟵
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi id
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mi e
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi ℓ
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi μ
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↙
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi r
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        1 \otimes A
                        \&amp;\overset{e \otimes id}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes A
                        \&amp;\overset{id \otimes e}{\longleftarrow}&amp;
                        A \otimes 1
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\ell}}\searrow
                        \&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mu}} &amp;
                        \&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{r}}
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; A
                        }
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                  are the left and right unitor isomorphisms of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              Moreover, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes , 1)
              has the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1, \tau)
              with symmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\mu, e)
              as above is called a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+in+a+symmetric+monoidal+category"} commutative monoid in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1, B)
              if in addition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  (commutativity) the following
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %munderover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mo ≃
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi τ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi A
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi A
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi A
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi μ
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↙
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi μ
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        A \otimes A
                        \&amp;&amp; \underoverset{\simeq}{\tau_{A,A}}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                        A \otimes A
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\mu}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\mu}}
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; A
                        }
                        \\,.
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of monoids
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_1, \mu_1, e_1)\longrightarrow (A_2, \mu_2, f_2)
              is a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; A_1 \longrightarrow A_2
            %p
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagrams commute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi f
                                %mo ⊗
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi μ
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi μ
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_1 \otimes A_1
                    \&amp;\overset{f \otimes f}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    A_2 \otimes A_2
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\mu_1}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\mu_2}}
                    \\\
                    A_1 &amp;\underset{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A_2
                    }
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi 𝒸
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mn 2
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    1_{\mathcal{c}} &amp;\overset{e_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; A_1
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{e_2}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; A_2
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(\mathcal{C}, \otimes,1)
              for the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CMon(\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              for its subcategory of commutative monoids.
          #MonoidsInVectAreAssociativeAlgebras.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              from example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorProductOfVectorSpaces"}
              is equivalently an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              over the given
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect
              is an ordinary
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              of monoids agree with usual algebra homomorphisms. Hence there are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences+of+categories"} equivalences of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mon(Vect_k) \simeq Alg_k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CMon(Vect_k) \simeq CAlg_k
                    \\,.
          #GradedAlgebras.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInVectAreAssociativeAlgebras"}
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
              from example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedVectorSpacesAsAMonoidaCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Alg_k^G \simeq Mon(Vect_k^G)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that a
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %munder
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mrow
                            %mi g
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \underset{g\in G}{\oplus} A_g
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
                  structure on the underlying vector space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              such that for two elements of homogeneous degree, i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1 \in A_{g_1} \hookrightarrow A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_2 \in A_{g_2} \hookrightarrow A
              then their product is in degre
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1 g_2
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_{g_1} a_{g_2} \in A_{g_1 g_2} \hookrightarrow A
                    \\,.
          %p
            Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInVectAreAssociativeAlgebras"}
            motivates the following definition:
          #SupercommutativeSuperalgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+super+vector+spaces"} category of super vector spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfSuperVectorSpaces"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sCAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sCAlg_k
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
              with the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              between them:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sCAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sVect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sCAlg_k \;\coloneqq\; CMon(sVect_k)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Unwinding what this means, then a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedAlgebras"}
              %li
                %p
                  such that for any two elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b
                  of homogeneous degree, their product satisfies
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi deg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi deg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi b
                        %mi a
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        a b \; = \; (-1)^{deg(a) deg(b)}\, b a
                        \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In view of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
              we might define a not-necessarily supercommutative superalgebra to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              (not necessarily commutative) in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sVect"} sVect
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sVect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sAlg_k \coloneqq Mon(sVect)
                    \\,.
            %p
              However, since the definition of not-necessarily commutative monoids (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              of the ambient
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              differ from
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
              only via their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              (example
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfSuperVectorSpaces"}
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedAlgebras"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sAlg_k \simeq Alg_k^{\mathbb{Z}/2}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence the heart of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} super-commutativity
          #GrassmannAlgebra.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} freely generated
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta_i\}_{i = 1}^n
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo •
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^\bullet \mathbb{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_i
              in odd degree, by the ideal generated by the relations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta_i \theta_j = - \theta_j \theta_i
            %p
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,j \in \{1, \cdots, n\}
            %p
              This is also called a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#Grassmann1844"} Grassmann 1844
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
              a century ahead of his time.
            %p We also denote this algebra by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi sCAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\wedge^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \\;\in\;
                    sCAlg_{\mathbb{R}}
                    \\,.
          #HomotopyCommutativeRingSpectrum.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+commutative+ring+spectrum"} homotopy commutative ring spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              (i.e., via the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized cohomology theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(E)
              inherit the structure of a super-commutative ring.
            %p
              See at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory
              in the section
              %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#HomotopyRingSpectra"} 1-2 Homotopy commutative ring spectra
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#HomotopyGroupsOfHomotopyCommutativeRingSpectrum"} this proposition
          %p
            The following is an elementary but fundamental fact about the relation between commutative algbra and supercommutative superalgebra. It is implicit in much of the literature, but maybe the only place where it has been made explicit before is (
            %a{:href => "#CarchediRoytenberg12"}> Carchedi-Roytenberg 12, example 3.18
            ).
          #InclusionOfCAlgIntosCAlg.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi CAlg
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi sCAlg
                              %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi CMon
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Vect
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %mi CMon
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi sVect
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    CAlg_k &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; sCAlg_k
                    \\\
                    \= &amp;&amp; =
                    \\\
                    CMon(Vect_k) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; CMon(sVect_k)
                    }
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInVectAreAssociativeAlgebras"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsPreservedByLaxMonoidalFunctor"}
              from the full inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Vectk
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi sVect
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i \;\colon\; Vectk \hookrightarrow sVect_k
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VectorSpaces"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfSuperVectorSpaces"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+functor"} braided monoidal functor
              by prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfVectorSpacesIntoSupervectorSpaces"}
            %p
              This inclusion functor has both a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              , (an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              exibiting a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
              inclusion, an “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+cylinder"}> adjoint cylinder
              ”):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi k
                    %munderover
                      %mo ↪
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi even
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi odd
                    %msub
                      %mi sCAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CAlg_k
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{(-)_{even}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{(-)/(-)_{odd}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\hookrightarrow}
                    sCAlg_k
                    \\,.
            %p Here
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi even
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_{even}
                  sends a supercommutative superalgebra to its even part
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ↦
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi even
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto A_{even}
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi even
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)/(-)_{even}
                  sends a supercommutative superalgebra to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
                  by the ideal which is generated by its odd part
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi odd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \mapsto A/(A_{odd})
                  (hence it sets all elements to zero which may be written as a product such that at least one factor is odd-graded).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The full inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is evident. To see the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
              observe their characteristic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijections"} natural bijections
              between
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi ordinary
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{ordinary}
              is an ordinary commutative algebra regarded as a superalgeba
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi ordinary
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i(A_{ordinary})
              concentrated in even degree, and if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is any superalgebra,
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  then every super-algebra homomorphism of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi ordinary
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{ordinary} \to B
                  must factor through
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi B
                            %mi even
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{even}
                  = succeed "-grading." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi sCAlg
                              %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi ordinary
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi CAlg
                              %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi ordinary
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{sCAlg_k}(i(A_{ordinary}), B) \simeq Hom_{CAlg_k}(A_{ordinary,B_{even}})
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  every super-algebra homomorphism of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo →
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi ordinary
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to i(A_{ordinary})
                  must send every odd element of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  to 0, again because homomorphism have to respect the
                  = succeed "-grading," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi odd
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{odd}
                  must be sent to zero, hence the homomorphism must facto through the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo →
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi B
                            %mi odd
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to B/B_{odd}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi sCalg
                              %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi ordinary
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Alg
                              %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi odd
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi ordinary
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Hom_{sCalg_k}(B, i(A_{ordinary}))
                        \\simeq
                        Hom_{Alg_k}(B/B_{odd}, A_{ordinary})
                        \\,.
          %p
            It is useful to make explicit the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
            perspective on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"} supercommutative superalgebras
          #Affines.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Aff(\mathcal{C}) \coloneqq CMon(\mathcal{C})^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+commutative+monoids"} category of commutative monoids
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in CMon(\mathcal{C})
              we write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spec(A)
                    \\in
                    Aff(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              for the same object, regarded in the opposite category. We also call this the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Aff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Aff(\mathcal{C})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O}(X) \in CMon(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              for the same object, regarded in the category of commutative monoids. We also call this the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #AffineSuperSchemes.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For the special case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} mathal
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathal{C} =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sVect"} sVect
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfSuperVectorSpaces"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Affines"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sVect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi scAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mi op
                    %mo =
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sVect
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Aff(sVect_k) = scAlg_k^{op} =  CMon(sVect_k)^{op}
            %p
              are
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+super+schemes"} affine super schemes
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          #OrdinaryCAlgAssCAlg.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}
              an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
              by regarding it as being concentrated in even degrees. Accordingly, via def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Affines"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+schemes"} affine schemes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} fully embed
              into
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+super+schemes"} affine super schemes
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AffineSuperSchemes"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Vect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sVect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Aff(Vect_k)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Aff(sVect_k)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^p
              an ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+superscheme"} affine superscheme
              in even degree, under the above embedding. As such, it is usually written
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sVect
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{p \vert 0}
                    \\in
                    Aff(sVect_k)
                    \\,.
          #Superpoint.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              The formal dual space, according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Affines"}
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Affines"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{R}^q)
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GrassmannAlgebra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+expansion"} Taylor expansion
              of any real-valued function on it become “so very small” as to be actually equal to zero, at least after the
              = succeed "-th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %p
              For instance for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = 2
              then a general element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{R}^q)
              is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 12
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f = a_0 + a_1 \theta_1 + a_2 \theta_2 + a_{12} \theta_1 \theta_2
                    \\;\;\;\in
                    \\wedge^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{R}^q)
                    \\,.
            %p
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 12
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1,a_2, a_{12} \in \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taylor+expansion"} Taylor expansion
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 2
                        %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∂
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    g(x_1, x_2) =
                    g(0) + \frac{\partial g}{\partial x_1}(0)\, x_1 + \frac{\partial g}{\partial x_2}(0)\, x_2
                    +
                    \\frac{\partial^2 g}{\partial x_1 \partial x_2}(0) \, x_1 x_2
                    +
                    \\cdots
                    \\,.
            %p
              Therefore the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
              to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              behaves like an infinitesimal neighbourhood of a point. Hence these are also called
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
              and one writes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{0\vert q}
                    \\coloneqq
                    Spec(\wedge^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{R}^q))
                    \\,.
          #SuperCartesianSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              Combining example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrdinaryCAlgAssCAlg"}
              with example
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Superpoint"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductsInAff"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+super+schemes"} affine super schemes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Spec
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℝ
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo •
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi q
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{p \vert q}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\mathbb{R}^{p\vert 0}
                    \\times
                    \\mathbb{R}^{0\vert q}
                    \\simeq
                    Spec\left(
                    \\underbrace{C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^p)}
                    \\otimes_{\mathbb{R}}
                    \\wedge^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{R}^q
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              These may be called the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartesian+spaces"} super Cartesian spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
              as the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              do for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supergeometry"} geometry of physics – supergeometry
              for more on this.
          #ParityAutomorphism.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SupercommutativeSuperalgebra"}
              %strong parity involution
              is the algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi par
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    par \;\colon\; A \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} A
            %p
              which on homogeneously graded elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              of degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi even
                    %mo ,
                    %mi odd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(a) \in \{even,odd\} = \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
              is multiplication by the degree
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a \mapsto (-1)^{deg(a)}a
                    \\,.
            %p
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1303.1916"} arXiv:1303.1916, 7.5
            %p
              Dually, via def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Affines"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+super+scheme"} affine super scheme
              has a canonical
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
          %p Here are more general and more abstract examples of commutative monoids, which will be useful to make explicit:
          #MonoidGivenByTensorUnit.num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+category"} monoid in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitor"} unitor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ell_1 = r_1 \;\colon\; 1 \otimes 1 \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} 1
                    \\,.
            %p
              By lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kel1"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
              product with unit the identity
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id \colon 1 \to 1
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes , 1)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+in+a+symmetric+monoidal+category"} commutative monoid
          #TensorProductOfTwoCommutativeMonoids.num_example
            %h6#example_9 Example
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C}, \otimes, 1)
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid+in+a+symmetric+monoidal+category"} commutative monoids
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_i, \mu_i, e_i)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \{1,2\}
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1 \otimes E_2
              becomes itself a commutative monoid with unit morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    e \;\colon\;
                    1
                    \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    1 \otimes 1
                    \\overset{e_1 \otimes e_2}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_1 \otimes E_2
            %p
              (where the first isomorphism is,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℓ
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_1^{-1} = r_1^{-1}
              (lemma
              = succeed "))" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kel1"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi id
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi id
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_1 \otimes E_2
                    \\otimes
                    E_1 \otimes E_2
                    \\overset{id \otimes \tau_{E_2, E_1} \otimes id}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_1 \otimes E_1 \otimes E_2 \otimes E_2
                    \\overset{\mu_1 \otimes \mu_2}{\longrightarrow}
                    E_1 \otimes E_2
            %p
              (where we are notationally suppressing the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associators"} associators
              and where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              That this definition indeed satisfies associativity and commutativity follows from the corresponding properties of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E_i,\mu_i, e_i)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BraidedMonoidalCategory"}
            %p
              Similarly one checks that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1 = E_2 = E
              then the unit maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi id
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi e
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \simeq E \otimes 1
                    \\overset{id \otimes e}{\longrightarrow}
                    E \otimes E
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mn 1
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \simeq 1 \otimes E
                    \\overset{e \otimes 1}{\longrightarrow}
                    E \otimes E
            %p and the product map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mu
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E \otimes E
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E
            %p and the braiding
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_{E,E}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    E \otimes E
                    \\longrightarrow
                    E \otimes E
            %p
              are monoid homomorphisms, with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \otimes E
              equipped with the above monoid structure.
          %p
            Monoids are preserved by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
          #MonoidsPreservedByLaxMonoidalFunctor.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{C},\otimes_{\mathcal{C}}, 1_{\mathcal{C}})
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{D}, \otimes_{\mathcal{D}},1_{\mathcal{D}})
              be two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidalCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LaxMonoidalFunctor"}
            %p
              Then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\mu_A,e_A)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+in+a+monoidal+category"} monoid in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A) \in \mathcal{D}
              becomes a monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (F(A), \mu_{F(A)}, e_{F(A)})
              by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mu_{F(A)}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    F(A) \otimes_{\mathcal{C}} F(A)
                    \\overset{}{\longrightarrow}
                    F(A \otimes_{\mathcal{C}} A)
                    \\overset{F(\mu_A)}{\longrightarrow}
                    F(A)
            %p
              (where the first morphism is the structure morphism of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    e_{F(A)}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    1_{\mathcal{D}}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    F(1_{\mathcal{C}})
                    \\overset{F(e_A)}{\longrightarrow}
                    F(A)
            %p
              (where again the first morphism is the corresponding structure morphism of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p This construction extends to a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mon(F)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Mon(\mathcal{C}, \otimes_{\mathcal{C}}, 1_{\mathcal{C}})
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Mon(\mathcal{D},\otimes_{\mathcal{D}}, 1_{\mathcal{D}})
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+monoids"} category of monoids
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            %p
              Moreover, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+categories"} symmetric monoidal categories
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetricMonoidalCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+functor"} braided monoidal functor
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LaxMonoidalFunctor"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonoidsInMonoidalCategory"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
